// name :
"P54936778" "The Widow in Red"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - TheAmberWidow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P209650734" "The Amber Widow"
// DetailString :
"P873110554" "This black widow spider was trapped in amber nearly a million years ago. It is perfectly preserved in a state between life and death. It is the perfect catalyst for the resurrection of the woman known as the Red Widow"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ThreeObols 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1422166635" "Three Obols"
// DetailString :
"P4048607994" "These ancient Greek obols, or coins, are what is used to pay the boatman Charon to carry your soul across the river Styx to the afterlife. Three of them should buy passage to the underworld and then a return trip for you and a... guest."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DyingBreath 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P914759286" "A Dying Breath, bottled"
// DetailString :
"P4114592732" "One of the most powerful reagents in a resurrection spell is the final breath of a sentient being. Often faked, and incredibly difficult to mass-produce, this ingredient alone holds the key to bringing someone back from the dead."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Ritual 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P196665962" "The Resurrection Ritual"
// DetailString :
"P892891898" "Complicated and incomplete, this ritual seems to be 80% strict adherence, and 20% improvisation. You deduce that the proper way to perform the ritual starts with the placement of a single obol into a magic circle. From here things get sketchy. Some sort of catalyst is needed for you to successfully use the Amber Widow, something to give it purpose. Charon's return trip must then be paid for in obols. Finally the Dying Breath must make it's way into the circle to hopefully interact with the deceased. Then, and only then, will the ritual be complete."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ArrowOfLove 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3915801712" "Arrow of Love"
// DetailString :
"P789190182" "This arrow once belonged to Cupid himself. It has the power, when fired through Cupid's bow, to make someone fall irreversibly in love with someone else."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - CupidsBow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3339967148" "Cupid's Bow"
// DetailString :
"P1738657987" "The famed bow of Cupid. When an Arrow of Love is fired through this bow it will cause the intended target to fall madly in love with someone else."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - AWIR_PartOne_Hero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WiRPart1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2337494069" "A Widow in Red, Part 1"
// DetailString :
"P2747073288" "Jessica Megan Duncan, known in the hero community as Ms. Liberty, approached you to undertake the task of reuniting Lord Recluse with his long dead lover, Red Widow. Her position in Longbow has given her intel from the PSYOPS division that Lord Recluse needs a calming influence in his life and that Red Widow is just the person to do so. You were tasked with assembling the ingredients and finding the ritual that would bring her back from the dead, and in doing so gathered the Amber Widow, three Obols (ancient Greek coins), a bottle containing a dying breath, and the ritual itself."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WiRPart2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2692614134" "A Widow in Red, Part 2"
// DetailString :
"P1805541710" "Jessica Megan Duncan, known in the hero community as Ms. Liberty, approached you to undertake the task of reuniting Lord Recluse with his long dead lover, Red Widow. Her position in Longbow has given her intel from the PSYOPS division that Lord Recluse needs a calming influence in his life and that Red Widow is just the person to do so. You were tasked with assembling the ingredients and finding the ritual that would bring her back from the dead, and in doing so gathered the Amber Widow, three Obols (ancient Greek coins), a bottle containing a dying breath, and the ritual itself.<br><br>Within the mountain where Lord Recluse and Statesman fought Longbow PSYOPS constructed a summoning circle. It was at this circle that you performed the ritual to resurrect Red Widow, bringing her back from the dead. And come back she did, not with love in her heart, but hatred. Hatred for Lord Recluse and a passion to kill him where he stood."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - WiRPart3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P3110418103" "A Widow in Red, Part 3"
// DetailString :
"P2654268183" "Jessica Megan Duncan, known in the hero community as Ms. Liberty, approached you to undertake the task of reuniting Lord Recluse with his long dead lover, Red Widow. Her position in Longbow has given her intel from the PSYOPS division that Lord Recluse needs a calming influence in his life and that Red Widow is just the person to do so. You were tasked with assembling the ingredients and finding the ritual that would bring her back from the dead, and in doing so gathered the Amber Widow, three Obols (ancient Greek coins), a bottle containing a dying breath, and the ritual itself.<br><br>Within the mountain where Lord Recluse and Statesman fought Longbow PSYOPS constructed a summoning circle. It was at this circle that you performed the ritual to resurrect Red Widow, bringing her back from the dead. And come back she did, not with love in her heart, but hatred. Hatred for Lord Recluse and a passion to kill him where he stood.<br><br>You then learned that because you used your own blood to bring Red Widow back to life, your life force has been temporarily tied to hers. Coupled with the fact that Arbiter Daos has put a death mark on Red Widow, in order to protect Lord Recluse, it's only a matter of time before her death would bring about your own. Fortunately, DJ Zero, the proprietor of Pocket D, had a plan for you to make Red Widow fall in love with Lord Recluse all over again. The bow and arrow belonging to Cupid were key in bringing her out of her insane state. You were able to steal the bow from Countess Crey and the arrow from the Carnival of Shadows."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - WiRSouvenirHero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P579104341" "You have kept the Amber Widow as a souvenir of the story you refer to as<br><br>The Widow in Red<br><br>Jessica Megan Duncan, known in the hero community as Ms. Liberty, approached you to undertake the task of reuniting Lord Recluse with his long dead lover, Red Widow. Her position in Longbow has given her intel from the PSYOPS division that Lord Recluse needs a calming influence in his life and that Red Widow is just the person to do so. You were tasked with assembling the ingredients and finding the ritual that would bring her back from the dead, and in doing so gathered the Amber Widow, three Obols (ancient Greek coins), a bottle containing a dying breath, and the ritual itself.<br><br>Within the mountain where Lord Recluse and Statesman fought Longbow PSYOPS constructed a summoning circle. It was at this circle that you performed the ritual to resurrect Red Widow, bringing her back from the dead. And come back she did, not with love in her heart, but hatred. Hatred for Lord Recluse and a passion to kill him where he stood.<br><br>You then learned that because you used your own blood to bring Red Widow back to life, your life force has been temporarily tied to hers. Coupled with the fact that Arbiter Daos has put a death mark on Red Widow, in order to protect Lord Recluse, it's only a matter of time before her death would bring about your own. Fortunately, DJ Zero, the proprietor of Pocket D, had a plan for you to make Red Widow fall in love with Lord Recluse all over again. The bow and arrow belonging to Cupid were key in bringing her out of her insane state. You were able to steal the bow from Countess Crey and the arrow from the Carnival of Shadows.<br><br>Armed with the bow and arrow of Cupid, you made your way to Grandville, dispatched several of Arbiter Daos' assassins and then was able to shoot Red Widow herself. When hit with the arrow she saw Lord Recluse and fell in love with him again. Unfortunately it seems that the leader of Arachnos was not calmed by being reunited with her, but was infused with even more motivation to take over the world, as now he has someone to share it with."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound1Hero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3342026479" "Ah, I've heard of your exploits, {HeroName}. What can I help you with?"
// Answer Text :
"P1064263112" "Tell me about obols."
// Answer Text :
"P3454156662" "What is an obol?"
// Answer Text :
"P2767241509" "I need an obol."
// Page TellMeAboutObols Text :
"P3760275831" "Obols? In magic they are commonly used in rituals that involve death and the afterlife, as Charon the ferryman to the underworld, would take an obol as payment to ferry a soul to the afterlife."
// Answer Text :
"P3268617410" "I need an obol for a resurrection ritual."
// Page WhatIsAnObol Text :
"P2091224497" "An obol, or obolus, is a name for an ancient Greek coin."
// Page INeedAnObol Text :
"P668811922" "You need an obol? Planning on dying sometime soon I assume? I can help you out, but tell me, exactly what are you planning on doing with said item?"
// Page INeedAnObolForRessurection Text :
"P853495704" "Good {Hero.gender=male Sir|Madam}, a single obol is used to pay Charon to take you TO the afterlife. If you want the trip to be a 'round-trip' I would suggest procuring multiples. How many souls are you planning on resurrecting?"
// Answer Text :
"P1787235125" "One."
// Answer Text :
"P1563504741" "Two."
// Page One Text :
"P915594232" "I see, then you would need two obols, one to send Charon across the river Styx and one to bring him back with the soul in question in tow. Is the soul expecting to be brought back?"
// Answer Text :
"P2600755362" "No."
// Answer Text :
"P2125116990" "I don't believe so."
// Page No Text :
"P892542746" "Then might I suggest a part of you take the trip as well, and for that you will need a third obol."
// Answer Text :
"P1178396712" "Then I will need three obols."
// Page Two Text :
"P3191528460" "Figured out you need to convince the subject to come back to the land of the living, did you? You'll need to send part of yourself in the ritual, and for that you'll need a third coin to ensure you make the return trip as well."
// Page ThenIWillNeedThreeObols Text :
"P379947004" "Excellent! Here you go, three obols. This should do well to bring back your friend, as long as they are willing to be brought back. A few souls prefer the afterlife to what they had here on Earth."
// Answer Text :
"P2654393589" "Thank you."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1872369894" "Hello again, {HeroName}. I bet you are wondering why I called you here of all places. I needed to put some 'distance' between you, me, and Longbow on this op, and Pocket D seemed like the right place.<br><br>Here is the situation: Longbow PSYOPS, you know, the guys who print up the flyers that say 'Recluse is lying to you' airdrop them over Grandville? Well, those guys also have been doing some psych profiles of one Stephan Richter, aka Lord Recluse, and came up with something very interesting. Longbow would love to task you and anyone you can wrangle into performing an 'off-the-books' op for us."
// AcceptString :
"P2050444605" "I'm game. Anything to disrupt Arachnos is good by me."
// SendOffString :
"P1076146164" "Excellent.<br><br>Spies and telepaths have uncovered more information about the woman known as Red Widow. Apparently she and Recluse were quite the item back in the day, until she was killed during a fight between Recluse and my grandfather, Statesman.<br><br>PSYOPS believes that if Red Widow was brought back into Lord Recluse's life his attention would be split. He would no longer have this single minded obsession with conquering Paragon City and the rest of the world. In a way, Red Widow can temper the beast that is my great-Uncle.<br><br>We will need to gather a couple things first in order to perform the ritual needed to bring her back to life. Fortunately the Circle of Thorns has a copy of the ritual we need, in one of their libraries we've been keeping tabs on.<br><br>In addition, we need you to get the following items: the Amber Widow, three ancient obols, and 'a dying breath.' Go and see The Conduit about the obols, Dr. Cheng about the Amber Spider, and you'll need to get the rest of the components from Orenbega."
// TaskTitle :
"P771651249" "<color deepskyblue>The Widow in Red</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2770291627" "<color deepskyblue>Part One</color>"

