// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page 1 Text :
"P3090950390" "This is the magic circle that the agent set up for you. This is where you will perform the ritual to bring Red Widow back to life. Performing the ritual wrong could have negative circumstances, but the ritual is incomplete and you will be forced to improvise. How do you want to begin?"
// Answer Text :
"P4041171137" "Start with the obols"
// Answer Text :
"P2657058419" "Start with the Amber Widow"
// Answer Text :
"P336378753" "Start with the dying breath"
// Page 7 Text :
"P3835091426" "As you contemplate opening the bottle containing a dying man's last breath, Ms. Liberty's words ring in your memory: 'One thing I can assure you though, is use the Dying Breath as the last thing, and only if everything else seems like it is working up to that point.' You think better of it and try something else."
// Page 12 Text :
"P876970117" "You place the Amber Widow within the circle, and nothing happens. No magic sparks, no gut instinct, just... nothing. Obviously this is not the way to start the ritual."
// Answer Text :
"P4151535095" "Start with the Obols"
// Answer Text :
"P1758448104" "Start with the Dying Breath"
// Page 17 Text :
"P306507862" "You hold three obols in your hand. You can place one, two or all of them into the magic circle. What do you do?"
// Answer Text :
"P3777525604" "Place one obol in the circle."
// Answer Text :
"P2984433395" "Place two obols in the circle."
// Answer Text :
"P3901194991" "Place all three obols in the circle."
// Page 23 Text :
"P1974903388" "The magic circle flares to life. The runes take on an otherworldly glow. You sense the boatman, Charon, awaiting a soul, a soul that has been paid for."
// Answer Text :
"P2733538404" "Place the Amber Widow into the circle"
// Answer Text :
"P2780799361" "Uncork the bottle containing the dying breath."
// Answer Text :
"P2859236762" "Let's start improvising."
// Page 29 Text :
"P2215675191" "You gather two obols and place them into the circle. Your gut kicks in with that sensation you get when you overpay for something."
// Answer Text :
"P4152269119" "Remove an obol"
// Answer Text :
"P1310419629" "Place the third obol in the circle as well."
// Page 34 Text :
"P3997948370" "All three obols are placed within the circle. You have the overwhelming sensation that you are being ripped off."
// Answer Text :
"P2957703662" "Remove all the obols."
// Answer Text :
"P1530294557" "Remove two obols."
// Answer Text :
"P2952498548" "Remove one obol."
// Page 40 Text :
"P1378979337" "You start over from scratch. Where do you wish to begin anew?"
// Page 46 Text :
"P4032662340" "Only two obols lay within the circle. Your gut kicks in with that sensation you get when you overpay for something."
// Page 51 Text :
"P2220144729" "You place the Amber Widow into the circle. You have an uncomfortable feeling that Charon is confused. He was looking for a living soul to ferry across the river Styx."
// Page 60 Text :
"P3244512565" "You've fought enough magic slinging enemies in your time, you should be able to fake this, right? Some ideas pop into your head: using magic incantations you've overheard in the past, cutting yourself and bleeding into the magic circle, dance around the circle, chanting a magical mantra, or light some incense and see what happens."
// Answer Text :
"P2675442499" "Start muttering some magic incantations"
// Answer Text :
"P2030944591" "Cut yourself and bleed into the circle"
// Answer Text :
"P268315291" "Dance around the circle, chanting"
// Answer Text :
"P3442711335" "Light some incense"
// Page 67 Text :
"P1448202134" "You raise your hands into the air and begin chanting magical words you have overheard in the past. <br><br>Suddenly you find yourself wracked with pain! It doesn't seem to subside when you stop chanting either! The glow of the circle dies out. You'll likely need to restart the ritual to progress."
// Answer Text :
"P2778676403" "Restart the Ritual"
// Page 71 Text :
"P3970233807" "You begin to dance around the circle, chanting a mantra you've heard used in the past. <br><br>Suddenly you find yourself wracked with pain! It doesn't seem to subside when you stop chanting either! The glow of the circle dies out. You'll likely need to restart the ritual to progress."
// Page 75 Text :
"P252534514" "You ignite a match and light some incense, other than adding a particular odor to the air, nothing magical happens. It seems you didn't mess anything up though, so you decide to try something else. "
// Page 81 Text :
"P892467835" "Your blood hits the ground within the circle and seeps into the soil as if it were a sponge. Only a dark stain remains where your blood once pooled. The magic circle grows in intensity. Charon seems pleased and the ritual seems to move forward."
// Answer Text :
"P3786058328" "Place the Amber Widow into the circle."
// Answer Text :
"P1680698146" "Let's continue to improvise."
// Page 87 Text :
"P907309459" "You place the Amber Widow onto the dark patch left by your blood. The fossilized sap seems to shimmer and begin to return to a liquid state, but still holds its shape. The Widow inside seems to be struggling to be freed."
// Answer Text :
"P470737450" "Place one more obol onto the circle."
// Answer Text :
"P308921292" "Place two more obols onto the circle."
// Page 94 Text :
"P2599541537" "As you contemplate opening the bottle containing a dying man's last breath, Ms. Liberty's words ring in your memory: 'One thing I can assure you though, is use the Dying Breath as the last thing, and only if everything else seems like it is working up to that point.' Since you haven't used the Amber Widow yet, it might be a good time to try that."
// Page 99 Text :
"P619893057" "That worked well, maybe you should continue down that path?"
// Answer Text :
"P235956117" "Light some incense."
// Answer Text :
"P3526365810" "Maybe I should stop improvising, this is getting nowhere."
// Page 111 Text :
"P3929642489" "With that thought in mind, you look to the remaining ingredients in your hands, the bottle of dying breath and two remaining obols."
// Page 117 Text :
"P3841008389" "You place down the obol. You get the sense that Charon is confused. The magic circle begins to fade. Quickly: what do you do?"
// Answer Text :
"P3338872678" "Place the last obol onto the circle!"
// Page 122 Text :
"P2649553522" "With both obols in the circle you see the image of Red Widow begin to materialize. She seems to be gasping for air and none is coming. This is likely the last part of the ritual, what do you do?"
// Answer Text :
"P3849459734" "Time for some more improvisation!"
// Page 127 Text :
"P1843967830" "As you contemplate opening the bottle containing a dying man's last breath, Ms. Liberty's words ring in your memory: 'One thing I can assure you though, is use the Dying Breath as the last thing, and only if everything else seems like it is working up to that point.' The remaining obols still need to be used."
// Page 133 Text :
"P1200412856" "Your mind scrambles to come up with something else to do when the image of Red Widow fades from view... Suddenly you are wracked with pain! Something has gone wrong with the ritual and the magic circle's energies die out."
// Answer Text :
"P3561318525" "Start over."
// Page 136 Text :
"P835870505" "The cold of the air in the cave condenses the breath as it is released. The image of Red Widow stands before you, taking in a deep breath. As it does, she solidifies into a living, breathing, human being again."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page 137 Text :
"P459199168" "As you contemplate opening the bottle containing a dying man's last breath, Ms. Liberty's words ring in your memory: 'One thing I can assure you though, is use the Dying Breath as the last thing, and only if everything else seems like it is working up to that point.' The remaining obol still needs to be used."

