// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SaysList :
"P3636037777" "<face=audience>LIFE! Thanks to you, {HeroName}, I can kill the man who let me die! I AM COMING FOR YOU LORD RECLUSE! FEEL MY WRATH!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - AI_INACTIVE 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - AI_ACTIVE 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3032661869" "You've brought Red Widow back to the land of the living, but at what price?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P642016583" "I'm glad Red Widow didn't just kill you when she came back. Perhaps she was thankful for you bringing her back?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Compound3Hero 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DJZeroTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page 1 Text :
"P3170679621" "I see you've gotten yourself into quite a pickle. Resurrecting Red Widow in the way that you did bonded your life-force to hers. What made you think using your own blood was a good idea?"
// Answer Text :
"P3928770224" "Nothing else was working."
// Answer Text :
"P3282831360" "Seemed like an obvious choice."
// Answer Text :
"P2902663627" "I don't want to talk about it."
// Page 7 Text :
"P3770170010" "Hmm, there had to be another way, but that is the past, let's talk about how we solve your current predicament. With Arbiter Daos putting a contract out on her, every cold-blooded assassin in the Rogue Isles will be hunting for her head. And if she dies, you die, for the time being anyway."
// Answer Text :
"P2218264401" "So I heard."
// Answer Text :
"P3571201687" "What do you mean 'for the time being'?"
// Page 17 Text :
"P2921391844" "I do know a way to perhaps stack the odds more in your favor... have you ever heard of Cupid?"
// Answer Text :
"P3714768272" "Of course I have. Everyone has."
// Answer Text :
"P1329767872" "Enlighten me."
// Page 22 Text :
"P2784044527" "Well blood magic is finicky. That kind of magic would be completely useless if the side effects were permanent in nature. No one would ever use it! The bound life-forces is only temporary, and should wear off in a couple weeks. Unfortunately you don't have weeks. Someone, or more likely a group of someones, will kill Red Widow long before that side effect wears off. Killing you in the process."
// Answer Text :
"P3098954889" "Great, but what can we do NOW?"
// Page 26 Text :
"P779307860" "Cupid. At least that's what the Romans called him. Son of Venus and Mars. Has a bow that fires arrows that make you fall in love."
// Answer Text :
"P2047308821" "Wait. What was that last part?"
// Page 30 Text :
"P3010988221" "So I take it you know why I bring it up then. What Cupid can do to solve your... predicament."
// Answer Text :
"P1810166472" "He does have those special arrows and that bow."
// Page 34 Text :
"P868784581" "Exactly. Cupid's bow, and especially his arrows. Get hit with that and fall madly in love with the next person you see. Now, get Red Widow into a room with Lord Recluse, fire this bow and BAM. Instant love connection, you don't even need to be back in two and two. That should mellow her out right then and there, rekindle that spark that was lost, and hopefully accomplish what you set out to do in the first place, reunite her with Lord Recluse."
// Answer Text :
"P4258079232" "Where can I find Cupid?"
// Page 38 Text :
"P2512869720" "That... isn't relevant. Cupid is LONG since retired, but his bow and an arrow are in the hands of private collectors."
// Answer Text :
"P2940795429" "Who? Who has these items?"
// Page 42 Text :
"P704905236" "Vanessa DeVore, the leader of the Carnival of Shadows, is currently in possession of the only known 'Arrow of Love.' Apparently they scratch themselves with it, using it as an aphrodisiac in some of their wilder parties. And the bow needed to fire such a special missile is in the possession of one Julianne Thompson, who your world knows as the person running around under the guise of 'Countess Crey.'"
// Answer Text :
"P324559545" "Julianne Thompson?"
// Answer Text :
"P3721099114" "So I just need to get the arrow from the Carnival and the bow from Crey, got it."
// Page 47 Text :
"P916067044" "Oh, you haven't learned that yet? Forget I said anything. It's hard to keep track of what is still secret in your dimension and what everyone knows."
// Page 51 Text :
"P1663981935" "You're likely going to have to take these objects against their owners' wills."
// Answer Text :
"P2339560503" "Got it, thanks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3836424419" "{HeroName}, well that last mission didn't go as well as we planned. Pretty much it was an unmitigated disaster if you ask me. Red Widow is alive, and apparently insane and just as deadly as ever.<br><br>There is a problem though... one that concerns your health and well-being. It seems that Arbiter Daos has put a death-mark on Red Widow, in order to prevent her from killing Lord Recluse. Normally in this situation, we'd just sit back and let the chips fall where they may, except HERE we have a hiccup.<br><br>It seems that your blood was part of the ritual to bring Red Widow back to life. The blood-bond isn't going to fade any time in the immediate future. If Arbiter Daos succeeds at re-killing Red Widow, you're going to die as well."
// AcceptString :
"P1652243857" "Me? I'm going to die?"
// SendOffString :
"P2270897668" "Yes, and I am sorry for that. However if you can soothe Red Widow's emotions before that can happen then the blood-bond can fade over time and Daos will call off his contract. DJ Zero has offered his help in this matter. I suggest you go talk to him and find out what he has planned."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2967923603" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three</color>"

